Package: baysesp
Title: Bayesian Accuracy of Multiple Diagnostic Tests under Partial Verification
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Giovanni", "Tinervia", , "giovannitinervia9@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bayesian estimation of the sensitivity, specificity and predictive
    values of one or more binary diagnostic tests performed on the same subjects,
    when the disease status is ascertained by the reference standard only for a
    subset of subjects (partial verification). Supports joint modelling of K tests,
    accuracy of combination rules (any, all, at least k positive), comparisons
    between tests, structured models for conditional dependence, non-ignorable
    verification and explicit sensitivity analyses for quantities that the data
    cannot identify. Models are written in 'Stan' and can be fitted with the
    'cmdstanr' or 'rstan' interfaces.
